# Computed Properties are Cached

When you call a method in the template, it **always** re-executes every time the component re-renders.

When you use a computed property, Vue **caches** the result. It only recomputes when one of its reactive dependencies changes.

```javascript
// This method runs on every render
methods: {
  getFullName() {
    return this.firstName + ' ' + this.lastName;
  }
}

// This computed property runs only when firstName or lastName changes
computed: {
  fullName() {
    return this.firstName + ' ' + this.lastName;
  }
}
```
